            <ArticleTitle>Low back pain and illness behavior (inappropriate, maladaptive, or abnormal).</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1522-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Patients with low back pain without a sufficient physical cause attract labels such as &quot;hysteria&quot; and &quot;hypochondriasis,&quot; often on the basis of exclusion. The concept of &quot;abnormal illness behavior&quot; was introduced to clarify the classification and diagnosis of these conditions, in which the behavior of the doctor plays a particularly important part. Principles of management are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
